      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MOSS-Image-Edit-HQ LoRA (armV3) on MOSS-Image Base\n\nNative ComfyUI nodes from [ComfyUI-Moss-Image-Edit-Native](https://github.com/PedroMarinhoDev/ComfyUI-Moss-Image-Edit-Native).\n\n**Models**\n\n- `diffusion_models`: [moss_image_base_int8_convrot](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/diffusion_models/moss_image_base_int8_convrot.safetensors) or [moss_image_base_bf16](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/diffusion_models/moss_image_base_bf16.safetensors)\n- `loras`: [armV3.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/akhaliq/MOSS-Image-Edit-HQ/resolve/main/weights/armV3/armV3.safetensors), saved as `moss_image_edit_hq_armV3.safetensors`\n- `text_encoders`: [qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors) or a bf16 Qwen3.5-9B (with its vision tower, which this LoRA uses)\n- `vae`: [flux2-vae_small](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/vae/flux2-vae_small.safetensors) or flux2-vae (same encoder)\n\n**Settings (tested on 14 edit types, see the README)**\n\n- LoRA strength **1.0**: lower strengths redraw the scene instead of editing it.\n- References and output the **same size**: reference_max_edge 0 resizes each image to the 1 MP size of its aspect ratio, output_max_edge 0 takes image 1's. Smaller references than the output zoom the image out.\n- CFG 3, 30 steps, euler / simple, layer 22 skipped on the negative pass (the official MOSS sampler default).\n- Empty negative, as both LoRAs were trained.\n- Both LoRAs were trained on SFT. On Base, text edits, subject replacement, hair and two-image edits fail more often: use the SFT workflows for those.\n- On fine structures it can overpaint: \"paint the bicycle red\" fills the wheel spokes solid red on most seeds.\n- HQ's text encoder also sees the images (the node puts them in the prompt, as ai-toolkit trains), and its colours come out more saturated than the source.\n- Example inputs: `example_inputs/` in the node pack, copy them to `ComfyUI/input`."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MOSS-Image-Edit-HQ LoRA (armV3) on MOSS-Image Base\n\nNative ComfyUI nodes from [ComfyUI-Moss-Image-Edit-Native](https://github.com/PedroMarinhoDev/ComfyUI-Moss-Image-Edit-Native).\n\n**Models**\n\n- `diffusion_models`: [moss_image_base_int8_convrot](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/diffusion_models/moss_image_base_int8_convrot.safetensors) or [moss_image_base_bf16](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/diffusion_models/moss_image_base_bf16.safetensors)\n- `loras`: [armV3.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/akhaliq/MOSS-Image-Edit-HQ/resolve/main/weights/armV3/armV3.safetensors), saved as `moss_image_edit_hq_armV3.safetensors`\n- `text_encoders`: [qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors) or a bf16 Qwen3.5-9B (with its vision tower, which this LoRA uses)\n- `vae`: [flux2-vae_small](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/vae/flux2-vae_small.safetensors) or flux2-vae (same encoder)\n\n**Settings (tested on 14 edit types, see the README)**\n\n- LoRA strength **1.0**: lower strengths redraw the scene instead of editing it.\n- References and output the **same size** (reference_max_edge 1024, output_max_edge 0); smaller references zoom the image out.\n- CFG 3, 30 steps, euler / simple, layer 22 skipped on the negative pass (the official MOSS sampler default).\n- Empty negative, as both LoRAs were trained.\n- Both LoRAs were trained on SFT. On Base, text edits, subject replacement, hair and two-image edits fail more often: use the SFT workflows for those.\n- HQ's text encoder also sees the images (the node puts them in the prompt, as ai-toolkit trains), and its colours come out more saturated than the source.\n- Example inputs: `example_inputs/` in the node pack, copy them to `ComfyUI/input`."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
  ],
